 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? Try using short clear lines, and give each one clear job. Start each one on the right side of center line, and end it on left. Then start each one on the right side of a center line, and end it on the left. Short clear lines look much more alive than long ones. Rough out rough sketch in pencil first, then hold it up against actual things. How does your drawing compare? Try turning your paper to side on, and draw right to left, like you' writing in short sentence. It feels strange at first, but it' worth it.",
